Temp utilities to test the whold Linux 3.0, including:

1. uboot image supporting device tree

Note uboot setting:
baudrate=115200
bootargs=no_console_suspend mem=512M console=ttySiRF1 retain_initrd earlyprintk
bootcmd=mmc read 0 0x3608000 0x3780 0x80;mmc read 0 0x02008000 0x1800 0x1800;fdt addr 0x3608000; fdt resize; bootm 0x02008000 - 0x3608000

2. flash.sh for flashing SD card
 example:
 sudo ./flash.sh sdc images

3. initramfs image
 3.1 basic busybox commands
 3.2 reboot, free, rx and other useful commands
 3.3 tmpfs mounted to /tmp

We don't free initramfs and use it as the real rootfs directly.

